  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.88:\n\t\t- Fixed: LogicMonitor has begun returning a role privilege objectType of \"agentic\", which\n\t\t  PrivilegeObjectType did not define. The enum carries a plain StringEnumConverter, which\n\t\t  throws on an unrecognised value rather than tolerating it, so a single unknown privilege on\n\t\t  a single role failed the entire roles or users response. Every caller reading roles or\n\t\t  users failed, whether or not it needed that privilege. PrivilegeObjectType now defines\n\t\t  Agentic.\n\t\t- Fixed: Role did not model the tenantIdentifier field LogicMonitor now returns on every\n\t\t  role. Debug builds set MissingMemberHandling.Error, so the response failed to deserialize\n\t\t  at the first role, before reaching any privilege; release builds ignore unmodelled members\n\t\t  and were unaffected. Role now carries TenantIdentifier.",
